TITLE:: ActionQMenu
SUMMARY:: A Button with a popup Menu for performing actions.
CATEGORIES:: GUI>Views, Libraries>jostMlib
related:: jostMlib, Classes/ActionQSubMenu, Classes/PathActionQMenu,  Classes/ActionMenu,Classes/PathActionMenu, Classes/Menu, Classes/MenuAction

DESCRIPTION::
A Button with Menu for performing actions.
Closes on unfocus or with esc key.



Supports Button or RoundButton  as a button classes.

If wslib quark is active, defaults to RoundButton.

Closes on click outside or on escape.


CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
Create an ActionQMenu

ARGUMENT:: parent
The parent view.

ARGUMENT:: bounds
A Rect

ARGUMENT:: name
The Menu Button Title

ARGUMENT:: items
An Array of link::Classes/String::, link::Classes/Association:: (\key->function), link::Classes/MenuAction::, or link::Classes/ActionQSubMenu::.

Note:: items

Use a String to trigger the defaultAction (and globalAction).

If a String starts with "-", it creates a menu separator.

Use an Association to trigger the associated function (and globalAction).

Use a MenuAction to customize all aspects of the menu, and trigger the associated action (and globalAction).

Use a ActionQSubMenu to create a sub-menu.
::

MenuAction will give you the most customizability.

ARGUMENT:: defaultAction
a default action for action items, in case no action is specified.

ARGUMENT:: globalAction
a global action which is run for any item.

ARGUMENT:: useDefaultFont
if your item is a  , override its font with menu font.
defaults to true. If you want to completely customize MenuAction items, set it to false;

ARGUMENT:: showArrow
show a little down-tick arrow, defaults to true


returns::
an ActionMenu



METHOD:: newMenuOnly
Create an ActionQMenu without the trigger button, so you can attach the menu to link::Classes/MainMenu::

See code examples below.

ARGUMENT:: parent
The parent view.

ARGUMENT:: bounds
A Rect

ARGUMENT:: name
The Menu Button Title

ARGUMENT:: items
An Array of link::Classes/String::, link::Classes/Association:: (\key->function), link::Classes/MenuAction::, or link::Classes/ActionQSubMenu::.

Note:: items

Use a String to trigger the defaultAction (and globalAction).

If a String starts with "-", it creates a menu separator.

Use an Association to trigger the associated function (and globalAction).

Use a MenuAction to customize all aspects of the menu, and trigger the associated action (and globalAction).

Use a ActionQSubMenu to create a sub-menu.
::


MenuAction will give you the most customizability.

ARGUMENT:: defaultAction
a default action for action items, in case no action is specified.

ARGUMENT:: globalAction
a global action which is run for any item.


returns::
an ActionMenu without the trigger button (for attaching to MainMenu)


METHOD:: buttonClass
Default: Button.

but you can use the RoundButton  from the wonderful wslib quark.

If wslib quark is active, defaults to RoundButton.


returns:: the Button class.



